<p>Mandan Creamery and Produce Company stockholders held their organizational meeting in the Commercial Club rooms on February 15, 1915. President {% person "william-a-lanterman" %}W. A. Lanterman{% endperson %} announced that the company would begin operating March 20 from the two-story brick Ronco Building at Fourth Avenue NW and First Street. Other officers included {% person "theodore-a-cummins" %}T. A. Cummins{% endperson %}, secretary, and {% person "hoy-sylvester-russell" %}Hoy S. Russell{% endperson %}, treasurer.</p>

<p>As a young man, Russell had worked at Hess Creamery in Glen Ullin, then one of North Dakota's largest creameries. He and his friend Henry Schulte moved their families from Glen Ullin to Mandan to manage and supervise the new operation.</p>

<p>Under Russell's guidance, Mandan Creamery and Produce grew into one of the nation's largest butter manufacturers and turkey processors. Mandan butter and turkeys were shipped and recognized across the country.</p>

