<p>Cloverdale, previously the local brand for the company's butter and ice cream, became its company-wide name during the 1970s as the business shifted toward premium pork products. Operations moved to a new $6 million plant northwest of the Seven Seas motel in Mandan. The plant held its grand opening in May 1988.</p>
